Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:13:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Co-op shoulders: per-station yields, shells still defer,
 geometry-hash proof

Review (REQUEST CHANGES): whole ridges held 250-1630 ms slices, each costing
a live crossing a 65-frame heartbeat payback (95.8 s build), and host shells
would have run ~20 s of unseen ridge work. Each ridge station now yields via
the world's own _build_breathe() (live build 60.6 s, worst slice 343 ms, no
extra paybacks); host shells keep deferring shoulders. The smoke now hashes
every ridge's transform and collision faces: live == solo, solo byte-
identical to main, and it checks the shell path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
